{"parentUuid":"b01064a8-9906-48d5-b81f-b8a16f0d5fc3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a00473bf11fbca24d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf23KqSB8vApvq7d4dv8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ey1LYzjrT3fAXTjZaCCaSD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/gps_report && cat README.md | head -120; echo ---; ls -la .env .env.example requirements.txt; ls -d .venv venv ../.venv 2>/dev/null; cat requirements.txt; which -a python3 uv; ls ~/go/bin | head; ls ~/.local/share/catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli/ 2>/dev/null","description":"README, venv, CLI presence"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6001,"cache_read_input_tokens":83346,"output_tokens":667,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":130},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6001},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":667,"cache_read_input_tokens":83346,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6001,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cf23KpNvKnB161e96mKdG","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"82ef03cc-06d1-47f9-8ccb-0a0a2b09fceb","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:06:37.507Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"764640dd-fa00-46b9-a4d9-f83074a06408","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"82ef03cc-06d1-47f9-8ccb-0a0a2b09fceb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"25464faf-de35-487d-80c8-05bd17310fd6","agentId":"a00473bf11fbca24d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ey1LYzjrT3fAXTjZaCCaSD","type":"tool_result","content":"# Baylor Football — Automated GPS Report\n\nGenerates a post-practice HTML report and email summary from Catapult OpenField Cloud data.\n\n---\n\n## First-Time Setup (do this once)\n\n### 1. Install dependencies\n\nOpen a terminal in this folder and run:\n\n```\npython -m pip install requests duckdb python-dotenv\n```\n\nPandas, Jinja2, PyYAML, and scipy should already be installed. If not:\n\n```\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### 2. Add your Catapult credentials\n\nCopy `.env.example` to a new file named `.env` (in this folder):\n\n```\nCATAPULT_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here\nCATAPULT_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here\n```\n\nFill in the real values. Keep this file private — never share it.\n\n### 3. Verify position group mappings\n\nRun this after a practice to see the exact position strings Catapult uses:\n\n```\npython run_report.py --list-positions\n```\n\nThen open `config.yaml` and update the `position_groups` section so each Catapult position string is listed under the right group name.\n\n### 4. Confirm your region\n\nIn `config.yaml`, set `catapult.region` to match your Catapult account:\n- `us` — North America (default)\n- `eu` — Europe\n- `au` — Australia/Asia-Pacific\n\n---\n\n## Running the Report (after every practice)\n\nFrom this folder:\n\n```\npython run_report.py\n```\n\nThe script will:\n1. Authenticate with Catapult\n2. Show a list of today's sessions — pick the right one\n3. Pull athlete data and store it locally\n4. Generate the HTML report and email summary\n5. Print the file paths when done\n\n**Output files** (created automatically):\n```\nReports/\n  YYYY-MM-DD/\n    report_YYYY-MM-DD.html       ← attach this to the email\n    email_summary_YYYY-MM-DD.txt ← copy this into the email body\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Commands\n\n| Task | Command |\n|---|---|\n| Run today's report | `python run_report.py` |\n| Run for a past date | `python run_report.py --date 2026-03-10` |\n| Use a known session ID | `python run_report.py --session-id abc-123` |\n| Check position strings | `python run_report.py --list-positions` |\n| Re-run an existing session | `python run_report.py --force` |\n\n---\n\n## Baseline Flagging\n\nThe system compares each athlete's session values against their own rolling 28-day average.\n\n- **Activates after**: 3 sessions per athlete (configurable in `config.yaml`)\n- **Default threshold**: 1.5 standard deviations above or below baseline\n- **Flagged metrics**: Total Player Load, Total Distance, High Speed Distance\n\nUntil enough history is accumulated, the report will show an informational note instead of the flagged athletes table.\n\n---\n\n## OneDrive Note\n\nThis folder is inside OneDrive. DuckDB (the local database) can lock if OneDrive syncs the file during a report run. If you see a file lock error:\n\n1. Pause OneDrive sync before running\n2. Resume sync after the report is saved\n\nAlternatively, move `data/gps_history.duckdb` to a folder outside OneDrive and update the `db_path` in `run_report.py` accordingly.\n\n---\n\n## First-Run Field Name Check\n\nOn the very first run, the script writes `logs/debug_first_response.json` containing a sample of raw API data. If any metrics show `—` in the report, open that file and compare the actual field names to the mapping in `run_report.py` → `parse_athlete_activity()`.\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n---\n-rwx------  1 kristinarash  staff  1379 Mar 13  2026 .env\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 kristinarash  staff   191 Aug  5 09:42 .env.example\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 kristinarash  staff    94 Aug  5 09:42 requirements.txt\nrequests>=2.32\nduckdb>=1.1\npython-dotenv>=1.0\npandas>=2.3\njinja2>=3.1\nPyYAML>=6.0\nscipy>=1.16\n/opt/homebrew/bin/python3\n/usr/bin/python3\n/Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/uv\ncli-printing-press\nespn-pp-cli\nfireflies-pp-cli\nflight-goat-pp-cli\nmovie-goat-pp-cli\nrecipe-goat-pp-cli\nzotero-research-library-pp-cli\nzotero-research-library-pp-cli.bak-20260901\nzotero-research-library-pp-mcp\nzotero-research-library-pp-mcp.bak-20260901\ncredentials.toml\ndata.db","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"238149c6-e4e7-4de5-b662-cd3c6325b753","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:06:39.104Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Baylor Football — Automated GPS Report\n\nGenerates a post-practice HTML report and email summary from Catapult OpenField Cloud data.\n\n---\n\n## First-Time Setup (do this once)\n\n### 1. Install dependencies\n\nOpen a terminal in this folder and run:\n\n```\npython -m pip install requests duckdb python-dotenv\n```\n\nPandas, Jinja2, PyYAML, and scipy should already be installed. If not:\n\n```\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### 2. Add your Catapult credentials\n\nCopy `.env.example` to a new file named `.env` (in this folder):\n\n```\nCATAPULT_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here\nCATAPULT_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here\n```\n\nFill in the real values. Keep this file private — never share it.\n\n### 3. Verify position group mappings\n\nRun this after a practice to see the exact position strings Catapult uses:\n\n```\npython run_report.py --list-positions\n```\n\nThen open `config.yaml` and update the `position_groups` section so each Catapult position string is listed under the right group name.\n\n### 4. Confirm your region\n\nIn `config.yaml`, set `catapult.region` to match your Catapult account:\n- `us` — North America (default)\n- `eu` — Europe\n- `au` — Australia/Asia-Pacific\n\n---\n\n## Running the Report (after every practice)\n\nFrom this folder:\n\n```\npython run_report.py\n```\n\nThe script will:\n1. Authenticate with Catapult\n2. Show a list of today's sessions — pick the right one\n3. Pull athlete data and store it locally\n4. Generate the HTML report and email summary\n5. Print the file paths when done\n\n**Output files** (created automatically):\n```\nReports/\n  YYYY-MM-DD/\n    report_YYYY-MM-DD.html       ← attach this to the email\n    email_summary_YYYY-MM-DD.txt ← copy this into the email body\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Commands\n\n| Task | Command |\n|---|---|\n| Run today's report | `python run_report.py` |\n| Run for a past date | `python run_report.py --date 2026-03-10` |\n| Use a known session ID | `python run_report.py --session-id abc-123` |\n| Check position strings | `python run_report.py --list-positions` |\n| Re-run an existing session | `python run_report.py --force` |\n\n---\n\n## Baseline Flagging\n\nThe system compares each athlete's session values against their own rolling 28-day average.\n\n- **Activates after**: 3 sessions per athlete (configurable in `config.yaml`)\n- **Default threshold**: 1.5 standard deviations above or below baseline\n- **Flagged metrics**: Total Player Load, Total Distance, High Speed Distance\n\nUntil enough history is accumulated, the report will show an informational note instead of the flagged athletes table.\n\n---\n\n## OneDrive Note\n\nThis folder is inside OneDrive. DuckDB (the local database) can lock if OneDrive syncs the file during a report run. If you see a file lock error:\n\n1. Pause OneDrive sync before running\n2. Resume sync after the report is saved\n\nAlternatively, move `data/gps_history.duckdb` to a folder outside OneDrive and update the `db_path` in `run_report.py` accordingly.\n\n---\n\n## First-Run Field Name Check\n\nOn the very first run, the script writes `logs/debug_first_response.json` containing a sample of raw API data. If any metrics show `—` in the report, open that file and compare the actual field names to the mapping in `run_report.py` → `parse_athlete_activity()`.\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n---\n-rwx------  1 kristinarash  staff  1379 Mar 13  2026 .env\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 kristinarash  staff   191 Aug  5 09:42 .env.example\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 kristinarash  staff    94 Aug  5 09:42 requirements.txt\nrequests>=2.32\nduckdb>=1.1\npython-dotenv>=1.0\npandas>=2.3\njinja2>=3.1\nPyYAML>=6.0\nscipy>=1.16\n/opt/homebrew/bin/python3\n/usr/bin/python3\n/Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/uv\ncli-printing-press\nespn-pp-cli\nfireflies-pp-cli\nflight-goat-pp-cli\nmovie-goat-pp-cli\nrecipe-goat-pp-cli\nzotero-research-library-pp-cli\nzotero-research-library-pp-cli.bak-20260901\nzotero-research-library-pp-mcp\nzotero-research-library-pp-mcp.bak-20260901\ncredentials.toml\ndata.db","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"82ef03cc-06d1-47f9-8ccb-0a0a2b09fceb","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"764640dd-fa00-46b9-a4d9-f83074a06408","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
