{"parentUuid":"a37588bc-6583-46de-8d04-9a066aaea21d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a00473bf11fbca24d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf23Uu7gR5t26dj1UJJYS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011xox8Fk9ec4yuBu4dpiXR7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/audits/2026-09-13-gps-locations.md | head -120; echo ---; grep -n -i -B2 -A4 \"refresh_all\" ~/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md | head -40","description":"Read existing GPS location audit notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4088,"cache_read_input_tokens":106113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4088,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cf23UtGL86zcs2AhatGPE","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"31c02e30-f565-4e91-9862-392b31942226","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:08:39.471Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"764640dd-fa00-46b9-a4d9-f83074a06408","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"31c02e30-f565-4e91-9862-392b31942226","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"25464faf-de35-487d-80c8-05bd17310fd6","agentId":"a00473bf11fbca24d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011xox8Fk9ec4yuBu4dpiXR7","type":"tool_result","content":"# GPS data locations and the one-home proposal (2026-09-13)\n\nAudit build 2. Eric asked: where should GPS live, and should we make a new location and\nremove the others? Read-only sweep of this Mac. Paths, counts and dates only; no athlete rows.\n\n## Proposal — no new location\n\n| Role | Location | Why here |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Mailbox** (raw exports, immutable) | GD `00_Primary_Storage_Drive/02_SPORTS/Football/FA2026/01_Raw_GPS/` (via `_INBOX` + `_Tools`) | Already where OpenField exports land. Documents sync through Drive. |\n| **Home** (the one queryable store) | `~/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/gps_report/data/gps_history.duckdb` (gitignored) | Only store with a schema, a writer and readers. DuckDB must stay off cloud-synced folders (lock trap). Rebuildable from the mailbox + API. |\n| Everything else | Readers or retired copies | — |\n\nA new single folder would put the DuckDB on Drive (lock trap) or raw athlete files in git\n(the `Catapult_API` problem). Both are worse. It would also repoint `coach_report` and\n`AgentAssist` mid-season.\n\n## The real problem is the pipe, not the folder\n\n- Newest DuckDB session: 2026-04-25. Last good import: 2026-04-30.\n- `run_report.py` pulls from the Catapult API (`src/api_client.py`, `CATAPULT_TOKEN` in `.env`).\n  It does not read CSVs. The token works: manual pulls on 09-06 and 09-07 succeeded.\n- The 20:00 runs from May to 2026-08-04 log \"Bulk import started\" and stop\n  (`gps_report/logs/run_20260804_200009.log`). No launchd or cron job on this Mac mentions GPS.\n- Suspect: Windows task `Refresh_All_Data`, left enabled at the 08-14 retirement, may be the old\n  scheduler. Check it on the next Windows session.\n- Everything from 2026 camp onward (08-25 → 09-04 practices, 09-05 Auburn game) is outside\n  the DuckDB.\n\n## Location map\n\n| Location | Contents | Newest data | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GD `02_SPORTS/Football/FA2026/` | Raw OpenField CSVs (25 practice, 12 walk-through), processed, coach outputs | 09-09 | **Mailbox — keep** |\n| `~/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/.../gps_history.duckdb` | 669 sessions, 47,361 athlete-session rows, 2020-08-08 → 2026-04-25 | 04-25 | **Home — keep, backfill** |\n| GD `05_SYSTEMS/DEV_Backup/BU-1979FJ4/.../gps_history.duckdb` | Backup copy | 04-25 | Keep — backup target, not a duplicate |\n| GD `02_SPORTS/Football/YoY_Camp_2024-2026` | Camp practice copies 2024–26 + processed | 08-27 | Keep — inputs to the YoY project |\n| `~/DEV/Catapult_API/` (private repo, 7 JSON tracked) | Only copy of the 09-05 Auburn game (68 athletes) | 09-05 | Copy JSON to mailbox, then untrack |\n| OneDrive `_MIGRATED_to_GoogleDrive/.../Football/FA2026` | Older migrated copy of FA2026 | 08-29 | Retire |\n| OneDrive `.../2026-03-10_DataBase_GPS_Reporting/.../gps_history.duckdb` | Old DB placeholder | 03-16 | Retire |\n| `~/.local/share/catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli/data.db` | SQLite, all data tables empty | — | Retire |\n| `~/DEV/Football/Tezino_CampPrep/data/tezino_gps_sessions.csv` | One athlete extract | 2026-06 | Reader output — keep |\n| `~/DEV/2025-11-25_EOS_Football_Analysis_GPS_ERR` | Finished 2024–25 analysis | 2025-11 | Finished project — leave |\n| OneDrive `PracticePlanning/Period Exports`, GD `10_ARCHIVE/2021/Catapult_PC_Archive` | 2025 and older exports | 2025 | Archive — leave |\n| GD `03_REPORTS/2026_GPS_Report.pbix` | Power BI, online dataset | — | Reader |\n| GD `01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-10_DataBase_GPS_Reporting` | Old copy of the reporting project, incl. 10.8 MB DuckDB placeholder | 03-16 | Retire (stale duplicate; sits in `_ACTIVE`) |\n| GD `01_PROJECTS/_DONE/baylor-gps-football` | Earlier GPS project: code, notebooks, SQL; no bulk data | 2026-02 | Finished project — leave |\n| GD `99_UNSORTED/From_Desktop/GPS_Data` | 89 CSV + 3 xlsx, FA23/FA24 camps | 2023–25 | Archive — leave |\n| GD `99_UNSORTED/From_GPS_Laptop/GPS REPORTS` | 197 PDF + 71 JSON, FA23/FA24 | 2024-07 | Archive — leave |\n| GD `05_SYSTEMS/Catapult_GPS` | 2 vendor PDFs | — | Not data |\n| GD `99_UNSORTED/From_External/FB_Report__GPS.pbix`, `From_Desktop/PostSeasonGPS_WinLoss.*` | Old Power BI and post-season sheet | older | Archive — leave |\n| OneDrive `PROJECTS/FB_FA24_GPS_SessionReport` | 271 files, 2024 season | 2025-07 | Archive — leave |\n| OneDrive shared `A.J.'s Projects/2025 GPS Dump.xlsx` | 2025 season export | 2025-09 | Not Eric's — leave |\n\nReaders of the DuckDB: `coach_report/src/data.py`, `AgentAssist/tools/archive.py` (read-only).\n\n## Flags (reported, not fixed)\n\n1. Catapult token in plain text: `gps_report/.env`, CLI `credentials.toml`, `Bearer.txt` in\n   FA2026 on both cloud drives, and possibly `GD/99_UNSORTED/From_Desktop/CatapultR_Tokern.txt`\n   and `09_Catapult_API.json` (existence only; not opened). Machine rule says secrets go in\n   Keychain. Worth rotating the token and keeping one copy.\n2. `Catapult_API` git history keeps the 7 JSON files after untracking. A history rewrite and\n   force-push is Eric's call. Repo is private.\n3. `~/.claude/scripts/backup-manifest.json` says `DEV/Catapult_API` is not a git repo. It is.\n   Manifest classification routes athlete data; change only with Eric.\n4. The catapult CLI binary is not on PATH, so `extract_tezino_gps.py` cannot run as-is.\n\n## Steps if Eric approves (none done yet)\n\n1. Copy the 7 Auburn JSON files into `FA2026/01_Raw_GPS/` and check the copies against the originals.\n2. `git rm --cached` them in `Catapult_API`, add to `.gitignore`, commit, push.\n3. Retire the four dead copies (OneDrive FA2026, OneDrive DB placeholder, GD `_ACTIVE`\n   `2026-03-10_DataBase_GPS_Reporting`, empty CLI SQLite). Archives stay.\n4. Next build: fix the import and backfill 04-26 → today into the DuckDB.\n---\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-46-\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-47-## Open questions\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md:48:- GPS: approve the retire list and the Auburn JSON move? Is Windows task `Refresh_All_Data`\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-49-  the old GPS scheduler? (Check on the Windows laptop.)\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-50-\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-51-## Gotchas\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-52-- Never commit a symlink into `~/.claude/skills/`. Windows pulls that repo and an absolute\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md-82-  because the task is disabled, not because it was repaired.\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md-83-- Three non-KeystoneOS tasks left enabled (`CFB-ForecastCaptureReminder`,\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md:84:  `DailyGmailDigest`, `Refresh_All_Data`) — all operate under the Windows `~/Desktop/DEV`\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md-85-  and touch none of the four repos.\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md-86-\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md-87-## Manifest classification — get this right, it routes athlete data\n/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_backup-sync-system.md-88-","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e78f4275-a14e-40fb-a12e-e9e99d503f4f","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:08:39.704Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# GPS data locations and the one-home proposal (2026-09-13)\n\nAudit build 2. Eric asked: where should GPS live, and should we make a new location and\nremove the others? Read-only sweep of this Mac. Paths, counts and dates only; no athlete rows.\n\n## Proposal — no new location\n\n| Role | Location | Why here |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Mailbox** (raw exports, immutable) | GD `00_Primary_Storage_Drive/02_SPORTS/Football/FA2026/01_Raw_GPS/` (via `_INBOX` + `_Tools`) | Already where OpenField exports land. Documents sync through Drive. |\n| **Home** (the one queryable store) | `~/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/gps_report/data/gps_history.duckdb` (gitignored) | Only store with a schema, a writer and readers. DuckDB must stay off cloud-synced folders (lock trap). Rebuildable from the mailbox + API. |\n| Everything else | Readers or retired copies | — |\n\nA new single folder would put the DuckDB on Drive (lock trap) or raw athlete files in git\n(the `Catapult_API` problem). Both are worse. It would also repoint `coach_report` and\n`AgentAssist` mid-season.\n\n## The real problem is the pipe, not the folder\n\n- Newest DuckDB session: 2026-04-25. Last good import: 2026-04-30.\n- `run_report.py` pulls from the Catapult API (`src/api_client.py`, `CATAPULT_TOKEN` in `.env`).\n  It does not read CSVs. The token works: manual pulls on 09-06 and 09-07 succeeded.\n- The 20:00 runs from May to 2026-08-04 log \"Bulk import started\" and stop\n  (`gps_report/logs/run_20260804_200009.log`). No launchd or cron job on this Mac mentions GPS.\n- Suspect: Windows task `Refresh_All_Data`, left enabled at the 08-14 retirement, may be the old\n  scheduler. Check it on the next Windows session.\n- Everything from 2026 camp onward (08-25 → 09-04 practices, 09-05 Auburn game) is outside\n  the DuckDB.\n\n## Location map\n\n| Location | Contents | Newest data | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GD `02_SPORTS/Football/FA2026/` | Raw OpenField CSVs (25 practice, 12 walk-through), processed, coach outputs | 09-09 | **Mailbox — keep** |\n| `~/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/.../gps_history.duckdb` | 669 sessions, 47,361 athlete-session rows, 2020-08-08 → 2026-