| older | Archive — leave |\n| OneDrive `PROJECTS/FB_FA24_GPS_SessionReport` | 271 files, 2024 season | 2025-07 | Archive — leave |\n| OneDrive shared `A.J.'s Projects/2025 GPS Dump.xlsx` | 2025 season export | 2025-09 | Not Eric's — leave |\n\nReaders of the DuckDB: `coach_report/src/data.py`, `AgentAssist/tools/archive.py` (read-only).\n\n## Flags (reported, not fixed)\n\n1. Catapult token in plain text: `gps_report/.env`, CLI `credentials.toml`, `Bearer.txt` in\n   FA2026 on both cloud drives, and possibly `GD/99_UNSORTED/From_Desktop/CatapultR_Tokern.txt`\n   and `09_Catapult_API.json` (existence only; not opened). Machine rule says secrets go in\n   Keychain. Worth rotating the token and keeping one copy.\n2. `Catapult_API` git history keeps the 7 JSON files after untracking. A history rewrite and\n   force-push is Eric's call. Repo is private.\n3. `~/.claude/scripts/backup-manifest.json` says `DEV/Catapult_API` is not a git repo. It is.\n   Manifest classification routes athlete data; change only with Eric.\n4. The catapult CLI binary is not on PATH, so `extract_tezino_gps.py` cannot run as-is.\n\n## Steps if Eric approves (none done yet)\n\n1. Copy the 7 Auburn JSON files into `FA2026/01_Raw_GPS/` and check the copies against the originals.\n2. `git rm --cached` them in `Catapult_API`, add to `.gitignore`, commit, push.\n3. Retire the four dead copies (OneDrive FA2026, OneDrive DB placeholder, GD `_ACTIVE`\n   `2026-03-10_DataBase_GPS_Reporting`, empty CLI SQLite). Archives stay.\n4. Next build: fix the import and backfill 04-26 → today into the DuckDB.\n---\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-46-\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-47-## Open questions\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md:48:- GPS: approve the retire list and the Auburn JSON move? Is Windows task `Refresh_All_Data`\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/docs/STATUS.md-49-  the old GPS scheduler? (Check on the Windows laptop.)\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/