{"parentUuid":"b9721cd6-76d5-4dc0-bcaa-d8d861d46b08","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a00473bf11fbca24d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf247ksrpBvhKn3of52A9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2739,"cache_read_input_tokens":152927,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2739,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf247jggD68pbXCxTbHpu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"26d0ac33-f473-4092-9941-51374cce9a7e","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:17:06.503Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"764640dd-fa00-46b9-a4d9-f83074a06408","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"26d0ac33-f473-4092-9941-51374cce9a7e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a00473bf11fbca24d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf247ksrpBvhKn3of52A9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# GPS import pipeline: why it stalled and how to keep it current\n\nThe code and the API both work; the scheduled run is what broke. I ran a live import against a copy of the DB and it pulled the 09-04 practice and the 09-05 Auburn game with no errors. Key columns were fully filled, 158 of 158 rows. The real DB was only ever opened read-only.\n\n## 1. How it works end to end\n- **`run_report.py`** is for one day and asks questions while it runs. It lists activities for a date (`GET /activities`), asks which session you want (`input()` at :289 and :312), then fetches stats with `POST /stats`. It writes to `sessions`, `athlete_sessions` and `athletes`, then builds `Reports/YYYY-MM-DD/report_*.html` and an email `.txt`. Because it stops to ask, it can't be scheduled.\n- **`bulk_import.py`** is the one that can run unattended. It makes one `GET /activities` call per day from `--start` to `--end` (:373-376). It keeps names with a standalone P or G, or \"Walk Thru\" (:34-55). It skips anything already in the DB by activity ID (:226), then does the same stats POST and inserts. It makes no reports.\n- **There is no CSV import path.** The reports that read the DB are `coach_report.py --date` (read-only), `AgentAssist/tools/archive.py` (read-only) and `compute_norms.py` (writes).\n\n## 2. Why it stopped after \"Bulk import started\"\nIt isn't hanging and it isn't auth. The HTTP calls have timeouts (`api_client.py:61`, `:85`), and the same token imported fine today. Every stalled log is one line long, which means the script died between `bulk_import.py:292` and `:342`. There are five ways out in that stretch, and none of them write to the log:\n- four `print()` + `sys.exit(1)` exits: config not found (:298), bad `--start` (:311), bad `--end` (:318), token missing (:338);\n- a crash when DuckDB can't open the file (`Storage()` :342, `storage.py:113`), which only reaches stderr.\n\nTask Scheduler throws away that output, so every failure looked the same. I reproduced two causes against a DB copy, and each left exactly that one-line log:\n- **Bad date (most likely cause):** `_INBOX/refresh_all_data.bat:13` builds `%TODAY%` with `wmic`, which newer Windows 11 builds have removed. Without it, `--end` becomes `~0,4-~4,2-~6,2`, exit 1.\n- **DB locked:** \"Could not set lock on file\", exit 1.\n\nTwo things point to the date:\n- On 04-28 a manual run at 17:04 worked and the 20:00 run failed.\n- `perch.duckdb` is fed by the same .bat with the same `%TODAY%`, and it stopped changing on 04-30 at 13:59.\n\nI can't confirm this from the Mac. On Windows, run `wmic os get localdatetime /value` and check the last run result for `Refresh_All_Data` in Task Scheduler.\n\nManual runs at odd hours also died this way (04-25, 04-27, 05-07, 07-16), so there is probably more than one cause. That's why the logging fix below matters more than the date fix. Also, a dropped network connection raises a raw traceback (`_get`/`_post` only check status codes) and would leave the same one-line log.\n\nThe scheduler was the Windows task `Refresh_All_Data`, which runs that .bat. It runs ForcePlate, then `bulk_import.py --start 2025-09-01 --end %TODAY%`, then Perch. Nothing on the Mac schedules it, and `CLAUDE.md` still says \"no scheduler, run manually\".\n\n## 3. What the API has\n- **Listing works in one call.** A single `GET /activities` for 04-26 to today took 2.3 s and returned 160 activities: 29 practices, 12 walk-throughs and 2 games match the filter. Camp P1 (08-05) through the 09-05 Auburn game are all there, plus PVAMU P1–P5 and G2 on 09-12.\n- **117 don't match, and you should check them.** Most look right to skip: summer `Group N`, `TEAM RUN`, `Conditioning Test`, `RTP - *`. The one to decide on is **`FC26 - MOCK GAME - 08.29.26`**.\n- **Backfill time:** each stats call takes about 1.2–1.75 s. With today's per-day loop, 43 sessions over 141 days is about 3–5 min. With one wide list call it's about 2 min.\n\n## 4. CSVs and the Auburn JSON\nThe API backfill is enough on its own, so the CSVs are a backup only.\n- **The CSVs** have a row per period plus a `Session` row, keyed by player name. They have no athlete ID and no velocity-band columns, so no high-speed or sprint distance. Layouts vary (120, 121 or 435 columns, one file with 9 extra lines on top). They'd need a new parser.\n- **The Auburn JSON** is a processed dataset with its own keys (`total_distance_yd`, `pl_per_min`), not raw API output.\n\n## 5. Recommended setup for regular pulls\n- **Owner: the Mac.** It has the most complete DB (669 sessions; Windows stopped at the same 04-25 date), the working token and both readers. The 11 `com.keystone.*` launchd jobs show it already runs local scheduled work. **Turn off the GPS step on Windows first**, or you'll end up with two DBs that drift apart.\n- **Cadence:** one launchd run each morning around 06:30 CT, which catches evening games. The same command also runs by hand after practice. launchd only fires if the Mac is awake, same as the backup. It's local, like the Task Scheduler job you already ran, not cloud — but whether that needs IT approval is your call.\n- **One command,** e.g. `gps_report/pull.sh`: import from the newest session date in the DB minus 3 days, then run `coach_report.py --date D` for each new practice date.\n- **Code changes:**\n  - Catch every error path and log it.\n  - Write a receipt after each run to `logs/last_run.json`: time, date window, imported/skipped/errors, exit code.\n  - Replace the per-day loop with one wide list call, and fall back to per-day if the list looks cut off.\n  - Treat network errors as `CatapultAPIError`.\n  - No lock file is needed: DuckDB's own lock already fails fast, so just catch that error and log it.\n- **Making failures visible:** have `claude-stack-doctor` read the receipt and flag it when the last success is more than 36 hours old.\n- **Files to change:** `bulk_import.py`, `src/api_client.py`, new `pull.sh` and `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.keystone.gpspull.plist`, `_INBOX/refresh_all_data.bat` (Windows), the stack-doctor skill, `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/STATUS.md`.\n\n**Security flag:** `API_Token_FB.txt` is tracked in git at the repo root. I didn't open it. Consider untracking it and rotating the token.\n\n## Fix list (in order)\n1. Disable the GPS step in `refresh_all_data.bat` or the task on Windows. (5 min)\n2. `bulk_import.py`: log every early exit, catch the DB-open error, write the receipt. (30 min)\n3. `api_client.py`: treat network errors as `CatapultAPIError`. (10 min)\n4. Add `--since-db` (newest session minus 3 days) with one wide list call. (45 min)\n5. Run the backfill by hand from 04-26 to today, after copying the DB as a backup. (15 min)\n6. Decide on the MOCK GAME filter; if yes, re-run for 08-29. (10 min)\n7. Write `pull.sh` (import, then coach reports for new dates). (30 min)\n8. Add the launchd plist at 06:30 and the stack-doctor receipt check. (45 min)\n9. Update `CLAUDE.md` and `STATUS.md`; untrack the token file. (20 min)\n\nAbout 3.5 hours in total. Items 1–5 alone bring reporting up to date.\n\nTest files are in `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/jobs/764640dd/tmp/gps-test/`: the scripts plus DB copies in `run_s1`–`run_s3`. `run_s3` holds athlete rows, so delete it when you're done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2739,"cache_read_input_tokens":152927,"output_tokens":2995,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":124},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2739},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":2995,"cache_read_input_tokens":152927,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2739,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf247jggD68pbXCxTbHpu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"763ef436-a495-4d36-81bc-604cfe16d527","timestamp":"2026-09-13T20:17:32.122Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS","sessionId":"764640dd-fa00-46b9-a4d9-f83074a06408","version":"2.1.270","gitBranch":"main"}
